# Sets

* (I): cakes (products)
* (J): sales channels
* (K): ingredients

# Parameters

* Prices & costs
  (p_{ij}): price of cake (i) in channel (j)
  (c^{\mathrm{ing}}_{k}): cost per unit of ingredient (k)
  (\tau_j): transport cost per unit sold in channel (j)
  (\kappa_i): packaging cost per unit of cake (i)

* Wages & oven running costs (€/hour)
  (w_{\mathrm{prep}},, w_{\mathrm{pack}},, w_{\mathrm{oven}})
  (r_{\mathrm{oven}}): oven rental (per hour)
  (c_{\mathrm{oven}}): oven utilities/energy (per hour)

* Technological coefficients
  (a_{k i}): units of ingredient (k) needed per unit of cake (i)
  (t^{\mathrm{prep}}*{i}): prep time per unit of cake (i) (hours/unit)
  (t^{\mathrm{pack}}*{i}): packing time per unit of cake (i) (hours/unit)
  (t^{\mathrm{oven}}_{i}): oven time per unit of cake (i) (hours/unit)

* Capacities / limits (optional but typical)
  (H^{\max}*{\mathrm{prep}},, H^{\max}*{\mathrm{pack}},, H^{\max}*{\mathrm{oven}}): available hours
  (D*{ij}): demand upper bound in channel (j) for cake (i) (units)
  (Y^{\max}_k): purchasable upper bound of ingredient (k) (if any)

# Decision variables

* Sales by channel: (x_{ij}\ge 0) (units of cake (i) sold in channel (j))
* Production: (q_i\ge 0) (units of cake (i) produced)
* Ingredient purchase/inventory: (y_k\ge 0) (units of ingredient (k))
* Hours: (h_{\mathrm{prep}},,h_{\mathrm{pack}},,h_{\mathrm{oven}}\ge 0)

# Objective (maximize profit)

[
\max \ \Pi=
\underbrace{\sum_{i\in I}\sum_{j\in J} p_{ij},x_{ij}}*{\text{Revenue}}
-\underbrace{\sum*{k\in K} c^{\mathrm{ing}}*{k},y_k}*{\text{Ingredients}}
-\underbrace{(w_{\mathrm{prep}}h_{\mathrm{prep}}+w_{\mathrm{pack}}h_{\mathrm{pack}}+w_{\mathrm{oven}}h_{\mathrm{oven}})}*{\text{Labor}}
-\underbrace{(r*{\mathrm{oven}}+c_{\mathrm{oven}}),h_{\mathrm{oven}}}*{\text{Oven run}}
-\underbrace{\sum*{i\in I}\sum_{j\in J} \tau_j,x_{ij}}*{\text{Transport}}
-\underbrace{\sum*{i\in I}\sum_{j\in J} \kappa_i,x_{ij}}_{\text{Packaging}}.
]

# Constraints

1. Production–sales linkage
   [
   \sum_{j\in J} x_{ij} ;=; q_i \qquad \forall i\in I
   ]

2. Ingredient feasibility (purchases cover usage)
   [
   \sum_{i\in I} a_{k i}, q_i ;\le; y_k \qquad \forall k\in K
   ]

3. Hour accounting (definitional equalities)
   [
   \begin{aligned}
   h_{\mathrm{prep}} &= \sum_{i\in I} t^{\mathrm{prep}}*{i}, q_i,\
   h*{\mathrm{pack}} &= \sum_{i\in I} t^{\mathrm{pack}}*{i}, \Big(\sum*{j\in J} x_{ij}\Big),\
   h_{\mathrm{oven}} &= \sum_{i\in I} t^{\mathrm{oven}}_{i}, q_i.
   \end{aligned}
   ]

4. Capacity limits (if applicable)
   [
   h_{\mathrm{prep}}\le H^{\max}*{\mathrm{prep}},\quad
   h*{\mathrm{pack}}\le H^{\max}*{\mathrm{pack}},\quad
   h*{\mathrm{oven}}\le H^{\max}_{\mathrm{oven}}.
   ]

5. Demand / channel caps (if applicable)
   [
   0\le x_{ij}\le D_{ij}\qquad \forall i\in I,\ j\in J
   ]

6. Ingredient purchase bounds (optional)
   [
   0\le y_k\le Y^{\max}_k\qquad \forall k\in K
   ]

7. Nonnegativity
   [
   x_{ij},, q_i,, y_k,, h_{\mathrm{prep}},,h_{\mathrm{pack}},,h_{\mathrm{oven}};\ge;0.
   ]

